    ],
    "solution_steps": [
      "Extract same-color four-connected nonzero objects against background zero.",
      "For each object, record its cell count, color, left edge, and top edge.",
      "Sort objects by left edge, breaking ties by top edge and then color.",
      "Allocate a black chart of height max(object area) and width 2*object_count-1.",
      "Paint one bottom-aligned colored bar of the recorded height in each even column; leave odd columns black."
    ],
    "source": "canonical.written_solution",
    "target_status": "source_written",
    "target_text": "Extract every nonzero same-color 4-connected object and count its cells. Sort objects by left bounding-box column, then top row, then color. Create an output whose height is the largest object area and whose width is twice the object count minus one. In each even output column, draw a bottom-aligned bar in that object's color with height equal to its area; keep every odd separator column black."
  },
